asset_intelligence:
Purpose
Network Asset Intelligence enriches the current NetMap baseline with services,
exposures, CVE candidates, risk, observations and recommendations.

Key principle
The current NetMap scan is authoritative for network observations. CTI, CVE and
other intelligence are enrichment layers. CAMT tools should therefore show the
same asset, service and vulnerability information.

Analysis & Advice can include:
- asset inventory;
- online/offline status;
- gateways and entry points;
- open TCP/UDP services;
- service exposure classification;
- product/version candidates;
- CVE candidates/confirmed matches;
- risk scores;
- recommendations.

Service Exposure Catalog
An open port is not automatically a CVE. CAMT distinguishes:
Exposure → Product Candidate → Version Match → CVE Candidate/Confirmed.

Examples
19/tcp chargen: HIGH exposure / legacy diagnostic service.
445/tcp microsoft-ds: HIGH exposure / SMB fingerprint required before reliable CVE correlation.

Reporting
Use Glossy Network Report with the same canonical analysis snapshot as the screen.
Diagrams, tables and recommendations should be generated from the same snapshot.

team_cases:
A central Team Case must be activated before case-bound data is published to Team Server.

Team Workspace
1. Open Team > Team Workspace.
2. Select a central case.
3. Choose Activate selected case.
4. Verify the status bar: Active Team Case: CASE-... — <name>

Publishable data includes:
- Network Asset snapshot;
- analysis/report payloads;
- provenance;
- module environment baselines;
- evidence manifests;
- additional revisioned case objects.

The local repository remains in place. Publishing to Team is not a destructive migration of local data.

evidence_store:
Large forensic files should not be stored as large BLOBs in PostgreSQL. Team Server stores the file in a separate evidence_root and records metadata in the database.

Metadata
- case;
- file name;
- size;
- SHA-256;
- uploader;
- upload time;
- MIME type;
- storage location.

Upload
The client calculates SHA-256. Team Server verifies the hash before registering the file.

Airgap import
Evidence from a .camtcase package can be transferred to the Central Evidence File Store after integrity validation.

Forensic practice
Keep original evidence read-only where possible. Use hashes to validate transfers and register analysis products separately from source material.

cve_dataset:
Local CVE Dataset

Open Tools > Database Manager > CVE Dataset.

Functions
- JSON import;
- online update through NVD;
- search local CVEs;
- product/version correlation rules;
- package rules;
- dataset statistics;
- controlled clearing of the catalog.

CVE correlation
A port number alone is insufficient evidence for a CVE. A reliable match uses
product, version, vendor, package/distro and other fingerprint information where possible.

Network observations
network_services and network_vulnerability_findings connect observed services and
CVE results to assets. These observations can be used for case-focused Team CVE Sync.
